ps://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tried this PR and it works functionally, but have a few usability / design remarks:\n\n- for usability reasons, can we somehow make sure that the floating point is much less jittery?\n\nThis is smooth and nicely readable:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/383a5745-1952-4221-a840-a4a6423b4ed3\n\n\nBut this one is jittery as it snaps to values, making it less readable:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cc0cdbc8-f32b-4084-9349-5b5827bf926b\n\n- can we also perhaps center integers slightly nicer above the key? this may conflict with the above option, but as far as I understand it, picking the 'seconds' view puts the animator in floating point mode and the FPS view puts it in frames mode, so perhaps you can force nicely centered integers in one and floating points in the other.\n\n<img width=\"165\" height=\"148\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c55c9d0e-b508-46c2-96b7-ffc88e146388\" />\n\n- not sure if this is related to this PR, but it could be: the snapping toggles seem to have the _inverse_ effect; they don't snap when blue (enabled), but they do snap when grey (disabled)?\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/571ac003-1de1-4f9d-a1ce-0ea58f886327","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117466#pullrequestreview-4050479437","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117466","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117466#pullrequestreview-4050479437"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117466"}},"submitted_at":"2026-04-02T12:56:56Z","commit_id":null},{"id":4054694064,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7xrbiw","user":{"login":"AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh","html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- When dragging multiple keys, holding the second key, and the first key snaps to `0`, it shows `-0` instead of `0` and the key itself it not visible on `0`\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d661386-d387-431f-981c-b6ea13be95f2\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117466#pullrequestreview-4054694064","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117466","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117466#pullrequestreview-4054694064"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/go